lisa-design:
- Base: origin/main @ b52a187 (R1). No git tags created (spec: consumers pin the branch pseudo-version). All four WPs (A1-A4) land in this one PR.
- go.mod: added github.com/google/go-containerregistry v0.21.2 (pkg/name only, R3). MVS bumped docker/docker to v28.5.2, which then resolved github.com/moby/go-archive to v0.3.3 and broke `docker/pkg/archive` (testcontainers, integration builds). Pinned github.com/moby/go-archive v0.1.0 (indirect) to keep `-tags integration` compiling. Consumers (agent) that also depend on go-containerregistry may need the same pin.
- ValidateOverlay is implemented as a hand-written strict schema walker over the decoded JSON (UseNumber) instead of private structs + DisallowUnknownFields: it yields exact RFC 6901 pointers and FieldError codes per leaf (R43) and treats every leaf as nullable without coercion. Behaviour is the LLD's O1-O11.
- Overlay bundle checks are PATCH-aware: ValidateOverlay (O11) runs the bundle shape rules on each non-null bundle patch but skips the two whole-bundle rules ("at least one of extends/modules/data", "delete requires extends"), because an overlay may patch a file-defined bundle. Those two rules run on the merged config (ValidateEditable against validation bases) and in the agent. The API pipeline runs the Rego-only checks via the extra exported regocheck.ValidateModules (ValidatePolicyBundles = ValidateBundles + ValidateModules, as pinned) on agentconfig.OverlayBundles(overlay) (non-null bundles, non-null string modules only).
- O6 plugin-name pattern is applied to non-null plugin entries only (a null entry is a deletion; deleting a legacy-named file plugin must stay possible). Bundle names are checked for every non-null bundle.
- Merge/DecodeConfig drop keys that encoding/json would match case-insensitively to a schema field without being the exact name (e.g. "Plugins", "plugins.x.Source") before the non-strict decode, so a miscased key cannot smuggle a value past the exact-name checks (found in self-testing). Unknown keys are still ignored (R51).
- PolicyOnlyChange step 1 uses a leaf diff that expands one-sided objects (first-time plugins.<p>.policies reports /plugins/<p>/policies, not /plugins) and additionally requires the set of plugin names to be identical in Merge(B,current) and Merge(B,next) for every base (an empty `plugins.x: {}` adds a plugin with no leaves). Conservative superset of the LLD rule.
- Server-side re-redaction of reports uses agentconfig.RedactDocument, which works on the generic JSON tree (removes api.auth.client_secret, masks key-name matches under plugins.*.config, plugins.*.policy_data, policy_bundles.*.data; keeps ${env:} values) instead of decode->Redact->re-encode, so fields a newer agent sends are preserved (R51). effective-digest is stored exactly as sent (R55); a change logs a warning.
- Redact masks a NON-string value under a secret-like key wholesale (objects/arrays included), per "non-string values under a matching key also become MaskedValue".
- PUT/revert order: 428 (If-Match) -> body decode (400/413/415) -> stale If-Match 409 (checked early, before validation) -> semantic no-op 200 -> D18 403 -> 422 pipeline -> CreateRevision (409 on race). A stale If-Match therefore wins over 403/422.
- AuthorizeAny under PDP-unavailable + fail-open lets the request through with NO action recorded as allowed, so the handler's D18 policy-only narrowing still applies (conservative).
- policy-author role = {"*": [read], agent: [read, configure-policy], playback: [execute]}: R53 says "viewer plus configure-policy", and viewer carries playback:execute on main.
- Builtin PDP: resource agent -> agent subjects allowed, users via evaluateAdmin (memoized with admin in Evaluations), anonymous denied (R39). No existing route used ResourceAgent.
- Agent-facing routes: /api/agent group with middleware.AgentJWTMiddleware (strict) + agent:sync; handlers additionally require agent_auth (401), so anonymous is refused even when Cedar grants anonymous the agent role.
- Heartbeat: only a well-formed config_digest (^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$) may register an instance; malformed digest / negative revision are treated as absent (last-seen update only), and the 201 is never affected.
- Instance cap + inserts: UpsertReport/TouchFromHeartbeat first UPDATE the existing (agent, instance) row; only a new row takes a FOR UPDATE lock on the agent row, counts non-prunable rows (R37) and INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE. ValidationBases/PreviewBases select only the columns they need (no policy_bundles/unsafe/errors payloads).
- ListRevisions overlay-size = octet_length(overlay::text) (jsonb text form, Postgres-only like BundlesFirstSeen); GET/revision DTOs use len(stored overlay).
- Prune job is scheduled only when cfg.Agents != nil && InstancePruneEnabled (LoadAgentsConfig enables it by default), on the "scheduler" queue, UniqueOpts ByArgs+ByPeriod 1h.
- sdk: executeStreamingRequest/executeRequest gained a trailing headers param; doRequest/doJSONRequest delegate to doRequestWithHeaders; Authorization in extra headers is ignored. AgentConfig.Get/Report return ErrAgentAuthRequired without a request when no credentials are configured.
- wire.go also exports PolicyBundleExtendsReport as an alias of PolicyExtendsReport (the name the agent LLD uses), plus Modes/AgentStatuses/Reasons vocabularies and AdminETag.
- Instance cap counts rows with `NOT ((daemon IS FALSE AND last_seen_at < oneShotCutoff) OR last_seen_at < retentionCutoff)`: `IS FALSE` (not `= false`) so NULL-daemon rows (heartbeat-only) stay counted exactly as PruneInstances keeps them. The LLD A2.3 SQL literally has `= false`, which drops NULL-daemon rows from the count after 24h.
- BundlesFirstSeen ignores bundle keys whose overlay value is not an object (a null bundle is a tombstone deleting a file bundle, not an overlay-defined bundle).
- ParseRevisionIfMatch accepts only canonical non-negative decimals ("0" or no leading zero, no sign): "+7", "07", "1e3" -> 428 (owner decision).
- WillApply returns mode-off/mode-report before considering forbidden changes: R23's "every mode" means every APPLY mode (owner decision).
- Preview forces will-apply=false/"invalid-config" for every instance when the overlay itself is invalid (overlay errors or error-severity policy errors), not only on per-instance errors, since the agent would reject such a revision.
- The LLD "A4 tests" line "only stale instances => 201 (standalone)" contradicts R48; the code follows R48 (validate against the latest reported apply-mode instance) and so do the tests.
- A report may carry a reason with status=applied; it is accepted (owner decision). The 4 MiB report limit is enforced by readJSONBody after auth instead of a separate BodyLimit middleware (same 413).

